{"context":"Anvil currently describes project, artifact, release, and runtime lifecycles, but it does not explicitly separate operations performed in a project repository from operations performed on a deployment server. This creates ambiguity about where runtime configuration lives, how projects are identified on a server, and which commands may depend on repository discovery.\n\nActual Sprint documents S1–S6 and Roadmap versions through `MVP-001-v4` are historical records and are not changed by this ADR. Source: ADR-013-server-runtime-context-and-registry.md Date:2026-07-19 Status:Accepted.","decision":"Anvil has three execution contexts:\n\n1. **Development context** — repository-aware, source-aware, and dependent on `anvil.yaml`. It produces Artifacts.\n2. **Deployment context** — transports and orchestrates Artifacts through published Runtime commands and contracts. It does not read Runtime Registry or filesystem layout.\n3. **Server Runtime context** — runtime-aware, independent of repositories and current working directories, and dependent on the server Runtime Registry.\n\nServer Runtime responsibilities are exposed under the `anvil server` command namespace:\n\n```text\nanvil server init\nanvil server project register\nanvil server release install\nanvil server release activate\nanvil server release rollback\n```\n\nRuntime configuration is stored on the server under `/etc/anvil`. Registered proje","consequences":"- Runtime bootstrap and multi-project server management become explicit product capabilities.\n- Existing repository-local runtime directory assumptions must not be extended into future work.\n- Runtime installation accepts a registered project identity and an Artifact, inspects its Manifest, stores it, and creates a Ready Release. Release activation targets that existing Release and extracts its stored Artifact internally.\n- Future planning must add server bootstrap, registry, registration, and server-scoped release command work items without rewriting completed work.","alternativesConsidered":"Alternatives see source doc."}